    "result_text": "All clean. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), computed on creation.\n\n**New shared helper** \u2014 `util/MembershipLevel.java`: `levelOf(owner)` starts at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 left reserved for tenure). This is the single source of truth used by both the mapper and the audit line so they always agree.\n\n**Response field** \u2014 `mapper/OwnerMapper.java`: swapped the `membershipTier` (`GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) mapping for a `membershipLevel` expression delegating to `MembershipLevel.levelOf(owner)`.\n\n**openapi.yml**: replaced the `membershipTier` string schema with an `membershipLevel` integer schema (min 1, max 3), so the generated `OwnerDto` now exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer has `membershipTier`.\n\n**Removed old tier behaviour**: deleted the household-based `GOLD` logic \u2014 `HouseholdMembership.java` and the `dto.setMembershipTier(\"GOLD\")` calls in `RespondWithOwner` and `RespondWithOwnerCreated`.\n\n**Audit line** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`: now records `membershipLevel={}` (the spec called out the create audit line as something that must record the level instead of the tier).\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The acceptance test creates an owner with a unique name + email and correctly gets `membershipLevel: 3` (1 + email + namesake0, capped at 3), and the audit log confirms `membershipLevel=3`.",
